  "can_do": [
    "I can say what I've got and haven't got — pets, things and family.",
    "I can describe how people look with <i>'s got</i>, like <i>She's got brown eyes</i>.",
    "I can ask <i>Have you got…?</i> / <i>Has she got…?</i> and answer with <i>Yes, I have</i> / <i>No, she hasn't</i>."
  ],
  "summary": [
    "<b>Have got</b> = I/you/we/they; <b>has got</b> = he/she/it.",
    "Negative: add <b>n't</b> — <i>haven't got, hasn't got</i>.",
    "Question: <b>have/has</b> jumps to the front — no do/does needed.",
    "Use have got for pets, family, possessions and describing people: <i>She's got long hair</i>.",
    "Short answers: <i>Yes, I have. / No, she hasn't.</i>"
  ]
}
